  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$\\int (4-3\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\,\u21d2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20616x & =\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-3\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u20616x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}\u20616x)+C \\\\  & =4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\u20616x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
